<title>GERMANY: Villeroy says sells Bamberger unit.</title>
<headline>Villeroy says sells Bamberger unit.</headline>
<dateline>METTLACH, Germany 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German tableware and bathroom fixtures manufacturer Villeroy &amp; Boch AG said on Thursday that it would sell its Bamberger GmbH subsidiary, which has annual sales of about 85 million marks.</p>
<p>Villeroy said it would sell the unit in a deal that takes effect on December 31, 1996, to the European firm Kaldewei.</p>
<p>The unit being sold employs 273 people and produces steel tubs and shower floors.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
